{"tool_name":"pgv","contents":["oeb","bioschemas","biotools"],"fetched_metadata":{"biotools":{"id":"pgv","home":"https://github.com/ucrbioinfo/PGV","license":"MIT","summary":"Reference-agnostic representation and visualization of pan-genomes.","addition_date":"2022-04-09T09:04:38.566731Z","last_update_date":"2022-04-09T09:04:38.569222Z","tool_type":["Command-line tool"],"accessibility":"Open access","biotools_curie":"biotools:pgv","cost":"Free of charge","credit":[{"email":"qlian003@ucr.edu","name":"Qihua Liang","orcidid":"https://orcid.org/0000-0003-3467-8103","typeEntity":"Person"},{"name":"Stefano Lonardi"}],"edit_permission":{"type":"private"},"function":[{"operation":[{"term":"Dot plot plotting","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_0490"},{"term":"Genome visualisation","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3208"},{"term":"Scaffolding","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3216"}]}],"name":"PGV","operating_system":["Linux","Mac","Windows"],"owner":"Jennifer","publication":[{"doi":"10.1186/S12859-021-04424-W","metadata":{"abstract":"\u00a9 2021, The Author(s).Background: The pan-genome of a species is the union of the genes and non-coding sequences present in all individuals (cultivar, accessions, or strains) within that species. Results: Here we introduce PGV, a reference-agnostic representation of the pan-genome of a species based on the notion of consensus ordering. Our experimental results demonstrate that PGV enables an intuitive, effective and interactive visualization of a pan-genome by providing a genome browser that can elucidate complex structural genomic variations. Conclusions: The PGV software can be installed via conda or downloaded from https://github.com/ucrbioinfo/PGV. The companion PGV browser at http://pgv.cs.ucr.edu can be tested using example bed tracks available from the GitHub page.","authors":[{"name":"Liang Q."},{"name":"Lonardi S."}],"date":"2021-12-01T00:00:00Z","journal":"BMC Bioinformatics","title":"Reference-agnostic repres